# Scratch / review artifacts — not part of the project record
onboarding-report.txt
*.scratch.md

# Local data store — the app writes here at runtime
data/

# A separate project that currently sits inside this directory. It has its own
# repo, its own database and real client data (tenancy documents, personal
# details). It must never be committed to Operator's history — this repo has a
# GitHub remote. Ignored rather than tracked; the proper fix is moving it out
# to a sibling directory.
Darams-CRM/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Python bytecode from the transcriber helper
__pycache__/

# Rust build output for the desktop shell. Hundreds of MB of compiled
# dependencies, regenerated by `cargo build` — the same reasoning as dist/.
src-tauri/target/

# Claude Code local state.
#
# `settings.local.json` is THIS MACHINE's accumulated permission grants — a
# record of what was approved at this desk, not a decision about the project.
# Committing it would publish one machine's allow list to every checkout and
# make one person's security posture look like a shared rule. Note that the
# `*.local` rule above does NOT cover it: that matches files ending in
# `.local`, and this ends in `.local.json`.
#
# `.claude/skills/` IS committed. Those are chosen, reviewed components every
# session on this repo should get — see docs/ecc-catalogue.md.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.bak
